{{!--
  OpenAPI contract template -- 19 §19.1's own "OpenAPI/proto templates" row. Renders an existing,
  already-registered InterfaceContract artifact (@forge/schemas' own registry) whose body embeds a
  real, valid OpenAPI 3.1 document -- no new artifact type or schema needed (see module.yaml's own
  header comment): InterfaceContract's own base front matter already covers "a frozen, machine-readable
  contract", generically, per its own base template's own prose.

  Renders against 19 §19.2's own real TemplateContext shape. `created`/`updated` deliberately render
  from `artifact.created`, NOT `now`: unlike fm-web's own two NEW artifact types (whose own schemas
  were written to accept a full ISO-8601 instant specifically because their templates render `now`
  directly, PLAN-M10.md P3 round 1's own fixed defect), InterfaceContract is an EXISTING
  @forge/schemas registry type whose baseFrontMatterShape types created/updated as a bare `date`
  (packages/schemas/src/registry/front-matter.ts) -- rendering a full instant into that field would
  fail interfaceContractSchema's own real `.date()` check exactly the way fm-web's own first draft
  failed its schema's `format: "date"` check for the opposite reason. `19` §19.2's own TemplateContext
  already carries a separately-resolved `artifact.created` field for exactly this: "resolved at
  render" by whichever caller populates the context, already in the shape the concrete artifact type
  expects -- this template trusts that contract rather than reformatting `now` itself (nothing in this
  codebase's fixed helper set does date-only truncation). A freshly-created artifact's own `updated`
  equals its own `created` at creation time, so both fields render from the identical value.

  Only Handlebars built-in helpers are used (#each, #if) -- no custom helper is registered anywhere in
  this repository yet. Every triple-stash {{{ }}} avoids HTML-escaping corrupting a YAML/Markdown
  scalar. The embedded OpenAPI document is fenced as `yaml` and is real, parseable YAML on its own,
  not merely well-formed Markdown -- test/fm-service-templates.test.ts parses it directly.
--}}
---
id: {{{artifact.id}}}
type: InterfaceContract
schemaVersion: 1
title: {{{inputs.apiName}}} API contract (OpenAPI)
status: draft
created: {{{artifact.created}}}
updated: {{{artifact.created}}}
revision: 1
author: {{{artifact.author}}}
changelog: []
---

# {{{inputs.apiName}}} -- OpenAPI contract

Owned by **{{{artifact.author}}}** for **{{{project.name}}}**. This file is the frozen,
machine-readable contract itself; delivery-guarantee and failure-mode notes for the interaction it
describes live in `architecture/integration/**` (integration-architect's own `kb_propose` claim), not
here.

```yaml
openapi: 3.1.0
info:
  title: {{{inputs.apiName}}}
  version: {{{inputs.apiVersion}}}
paths:
{{#each inputs.operations}}
  {{{this.path}}}:
    {{{this.method}}}:
      operationId: {{{this.operationId}}}
      summary: {{{this.summary}}}
      responses:
        '200':
          description: OK
{{else}}
  {}
{{/each}}
```
